          "filename": "Chinese Xin Shape Jewelry from Ming Dynasty Tombs.jpg",
          "caption": "This piece of jewelry was one of the most beautiful antiques excavated from the Dingling, Welcome one of the w:Ming Dynasty Tombs. It was made during the w:Ming Dynasty (1368–1644) in China, by using gold, ruby, pearl and other gemstones, and is about the size of an adult human's palm. It is of the shape of a Chinese character '心' (read Xin), which literally means heart. This photo was taken at the Dingling Museum.",
